  "names": {
    "order": "given family family",
    "conventions": "Everyone carries two family names: the father's first surname, then the mother's first surname (Ana Sofía Hernández López). In daily life people use the first surname, and women keep their own names after marriage. Compound given names are very common (José Luis, Juan Pablo, María José, Ana Sofía), and some families give names of Nahuatl or Maya origin (Xóchitl, Citlali, Itzel, Cuauhtémoc). Hernández, García and Martínez are the most common surnames in the country; in Jalisco you also meet many Íñiguez, Orozco, Navarro and Villaseñor.",
